---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const arrow = '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg>';
const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "AboutPage",
      "@id": "https://sportsperformancepsychology.com/about/#webpage",
      "url": "https://sportsperformancepsychology.com/about/",
      "name": "About Sports Performance Psychology: Our Mission",
      "description": "Why Sports Performance Psychology exists: clear, evidence-based guidance on mental skills, degrees, and careers in sport.",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@id": "https://sportsperformancepsychology.com/#website"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 1,
          "name": "Home",
          "item": "https://sportsperformancepsychology.com/"
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 2,
          "name": "About",
          "item": "https://sportsperformancepsychology.com/about/"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Sports Performance Psychology: Mission & Values"
  description="Why Sports Performance Psychology exists: clear, evidence-based guidance on mental skills, degrees, and careers in sports psychology."
>
  <article>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</p>
      <h1>About Sports Performance Psychology</h1>
      <p>An independent publication covering the mental side of sport: mental skills training, degree programs, and honest career guidance, all written in plain language.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Find the guide that matches your question</h2>
        <p>You might be choosing a degree, planning a career, learning a mental skill, or browsing the latest articles. Start with the section that matches your question.</p>
        <nav class="about-links" aria-label="Main sections">
          <a class="about-link" href="/degrees/">Explore degrees <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></a>
          <a class="about-link" href="/careers/">Explore careers <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></a>
          <a class="about-link" href="/mental-skills/">Learn mental skills <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></a>
          <a class="about-link" href="/blog/">Read the blog <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></a>
        </nav>

        <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
        <p>Search for sports psychology advice online and you will find two extremes: dense academic papers that assume you already have a graduate degree, and motivational fluff that promises results without explaining how anything works. There was not much in between.</p>
        <p>Sports Performance Psychology was built to fill that middle ground. The goal is clear, evidence-based guidance on sport and performance psychology for students, athletes, and coaches: what mental skills actually are, how athletes train them, what it takes to study this field, and what the careers honestly look like.</p>
        <p>Every guide is written with a real reader in mind and in plain language, without dumbing anything down. When evidence is thin or the answer depends on the situation, the article says so.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-author">
        <img class="about-author-portrait" src="/images/hassam-shabbir-author.webp" width="320" height="320" alt="Portrait of Hassam Shabbir" loading="lazy" />
        <div class="about-author-info">
          <h2 class="about-author-name">Hassam Shabbir</h2>
          <p>Hassam Shabbir is the author and evidence reviewer responsible for this publication.</p>
          <a href="/author/hassam-shabbir/">View full author profile →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>The final draft comes after the difficult questions</h2>
        <p>Every article on this site goes through the same editorial sequence. First, define the reader's real question and the claims that need evidence. Second, verify those claims against reliable sources, such as professional organizations, certifying bodies, and published data. Third, check the limits: what applies only in the United States, what varies by state, and what the research cannot yet prove. Finally, edit for accuracy and clarity so the result reads well without losing its evidence.</p>
        <p>The full process is documented in our <a href="/editorial-standards/">Editorial Standards</a>.</p>

        <h2>Clear guidance without false certainty</h2>
        <p>Sources are named and dated so readers can check them. Salary and program figures are presented with their source and date, because the numbers change. Where the guidance is general and professional judgment or further training is needed, the article says so rather than pretending certainty.</p>
        <p>An important boundary: this site is educational. It covers mental performance skills for healthy athletes and performers. It is not clinical advice, and the author is not a licensed clinician. Our <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> explains this in full.</p>
        <p>Corrections are welcome. If you spot an error, an outdated figure, or a statement that needs more context, please send it through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> so the record can be fixed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Subscribe band -->
  <section class="subscribe">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="subscribe-grid">
        <div class="subscribe-media">
          <img src="/images/runner-flexibility-warmup.webp" alt="Runner stretching on a track at sunset" width="1408" height="704" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="subscribe-copy">
          <h2>Get Sports Psychology Guides and Updates</h2>
          <p>Join our email list for new articles, in-depth guides, and practical resources on sports performance psychology.</p>
          <form class="subscribe-form" action="#" method="post">
            <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="Enter your email address" aria-label="Email address" required />
            <button class="btn btn-red" type="submit">Subscribe <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></button>
          </form>
          <p class="subscribe-note">Thanks for subscribing. You are on the list.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="keep-exploring-title">Keep exploring</h2>
      <nav class="about-links" aria-label="Keep exploring">
        <a class="about-link" href="/degrees/">Degrees <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></a>
        <a class="about-link" href="/careers/">Careers <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></a>
        <a class="about-link" href="/mental-skills/">Mental Skills <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></a>
        <a class="about-link" href="/blog/">Blog <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></a>
        <a class="about-link" href="/author/hassam-shabbir/">Author profile <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></a>
        <a class="about-link" href="/editorial-standards/">Editorial standards <Fragment set:html={arrow} /></a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}></script>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 20px 0 8px;
  }
  .about-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    border: 1px solid #d8d0d0;
    border-radius: 50px;
    color: inherit;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .about-link svg {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .about-link:hover {
    border-color: #D62828;
  }
  .about-author {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    margin: 36px 0;
    padding: 28px;
    border: 1px solid #d8d0d0;
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: #faf8f8;
  }
  .about-author-portrait {
    width: 96px;
    height: 96px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .about-author-name {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .about-author-info p {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .keep-exploring-title {
    margin: 0 0 4px;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .about-author {
      flex-direction: column;
      text-align: center;
    }
  }
</style>
